    </header>

    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <section class="mb-12">
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">House clearances are emotionally heavy, logistically chaotic, and almost always under time pressure. Whether you are downsizing parents into a condo, clearing a deceased estate, or preparing a property for sale or rental handover, the last thing you want is to be hunting for cardboard boxes at three different supermarkets. Quinocycle supplies bulk used carton boxes from our Balakong yard — graded for strength, sized for household contents, ready for same-day pickup or delivery across the Klang Valley.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Sizing the Job — How Many Boxes You Actually Need</h2>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Studio or 1-Bedroom Unit</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Plan for 30-50 mixed-size boxes. Small boxes (350x250x200mm) for books, crockery, and electronics. Medium boxes (450x350x300mm) for clothes, kitchenware, and small appliances. A handful of large boxes for bedding and cushions. Add tape, bubble wrap, and a roll of stretch film.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">3-Bedroom Family Home</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Budget for 80-120 boxes. The temptation is to pack everything in large boxes — don't. Books in a large box becomes unliftable. Crockery in a too-large box rattles. Mix the sizes: 30-40 small, 30-40 medium, 20-30 large, plus 10-15 wardrobe-format hanging boxes for garments still on hangers.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Landed Property with Storage Rooms</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Landed homes in Cheras, Kajang, and Subang often have decades of accumulated storage — old documents, sports gear, garage tools, holiday decorations. Plan 150-200 boxes minimum and order extra over-pack stretch film. The forgotten storeroom always doubles your estimate.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Estate Sales & Deceased Estate Clearances</h2>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Sorting Workflow</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Estate clearances need a sorting station, not just packing boxes. Set up four labelled categories: KEEP, SELL, DONATE, DISCARD. Use different box colours or marker codes for each. Our boxes accept marker pen cleanly and many estate executors find this colour-coding alone saves a full day of confusion later.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Documents & Personal Effects</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Sensitive paperwork, photo albums, and personal correspondence go into smaller boxes that one person can carry. Don't pack a 30kg box of documents — the box may survive but the executor's back won't. Keep these clearly labelled and centralised in one room for the family to review later.</p>

        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-4">Items for Auction or Online Resale</h3>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">Antiques, jewellery, watches, and collectibles destined for auction houses or platforms like Carousell need extra protection. Wrap individually in bubble wrap before boxing, and avoid stacking heavy boxes on top. Photograph each item before packing for inventory and insurance.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-12">
        <h2 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">Reselling Second-Hand Goods</h2>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface leading-relaxed mb-6">A growing slice of our used-box volume goes to second-hand resellers — Carousell power-sellers, Facebook Marketplace traders, weekend pasar lambak vendors, and thrift store operators in Cheras and Sungai Wang. Used boxes match the spirit of resale: lower input cost means higher margin per item, and customers receiving second-hand goods do not expect new packaging. Our Grade B boxes are perfect for this segment — sturdy, clean, but priced 30-40% below new.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="bg-surface-variant/50 border border-outline-variant/20 rounded-lg p-8 my-12">
        <h3 class="font-headline text-xl font-bold text-on-surface mb-6">House Clearance Box Estimator</h3>
